# Trivy CVE allowlist for dravr-platform image scans.
#
# Each entry MUST include:
#   - the CVE ID plus an `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` expiry, so an exception cannot outlive
#     its rationale silently
#   - a leading comment block explaining: which image, why ignored, when to remove
#
# An entry here suppresses the finding at the BUILD GATE ONLY, not in reporting.
# Trivy applies --ignorefile as a result filter before it writes its report, so a
# single scan carrying this file would hide the vulnerability from the SARIF too.
# publish-images.yml and publish-sciotte-image.yml therefore scan each digest
# twice: a reporting pass with no --ignorefile and --exit-code 0, whose SARIF
# goes to github/codeql-action/upload-sarif, then a gating pass with this file
# and --exit-code 1. An allowlisted CVE stays visible as a GitHub Code Scanning
# alert and closes itself when the upstream fix lands; what the entry buys is
# only that the publish is not blocked meanwhile. (Trivy keeps suppressed
# findings under ExperimentalModifiedFindings in JSON output; SARIF carries no
# equivalent, which is why the split exists rather than a single scan.)
#
# The expiry date is what re-blocks the gate: when it passes, the gating pass
# exits 1 again and holds the image publish until someone re-reviews.
#
# Scoping: the plain-text .trivyignore format understands an ID and an optional
# `exp:` date, nothing else. It cannot scope an ignore to a package, a path, or
# one of the three published images (server, frontend, sciotte), so every entry
# applies to all three scans until it expires. Package/path scoping requires the
# experimental .trivyignore.yaml format (purls / paths / expired_at), which the
# --ignorefile call sites do not point at; Trivy selects the YAML parser by file
# extension, so YAML written into this file parses as garbage IDs and silently
# ignores nothing.
#
# No nginx entries remain: the frontend CVEs that lived here (CVE-2026-9256,
# CVE-2026-49975) were patched at the source by switching the frontend runtime
# from the official nginx:alpine image (nginx.org's unpatched r1) to alpine's own
# patched nginx — see docker/images/frontend/Dockerfile.

# server + sciotte images: adm-zip 0.5.17 (HIGH, CVE-2026-39244) arrives with the
# GitHub Copilot CLI, pinned at 1.0.59 (newer CLIs regress the MCP bridge — see
# memory/copilot CLI regression). It is not inside the npm tarball:
# @github/copilot-linux-x64@1.0.59 ships four files (the SEA binary,
# package.json, LICENSE.md, README.md). adm-zip lands when the CLI materializes
# its sidecar tree at
# $HOME/.copilot/pkg/<platform>/<cli-version>/foundry-local-sdk/node_modules/foundry-local-sdk/node_modules/adm-zip,
# as a dependency of foundry-local-sdk 1.2.3; the `copilot --version` step in
# both Dockerfiles triggers that during the image build.
#
# Exposure, stated plainly: on the server image the CLI is the PRIMARY chat
# provider (PIERRE_LLM_PROVIDER=copilot_headless, infra/environments/dev/main.tf),
# so it spawns on every coaching turn — not on a narrow vision-login path. On the
# sciotte image it spawns for the vision-login LLM only.
#
# The suppression rests on adm-zip being unreachable, not on the CLI being
# unreachable. adm-zip's risk is extracting untrusted archives, and its only call
# site in foundry-local-sdk is script/install-utils.cjs — the npm install
# lifecycle script, which downloads a .nupkg and calls extractEntryTo on it.
# Nothing under foundry-local-sdk/dist (the runtime SDK) requires adm-zip, so a
# chat turn never loads it. That archive is named from deps_versions.json and
# fetched from a hard-coded feed list (api.nuget.org, then the ORT-Nightly Azure
# DevOps feed): no part of the URL, the filename or the archive bytes derives
# from athlete input, tool output or model output. Dravr runs remote Copilot
# models and never enables Foundry Local, so the extraction path runs only when
# the sidecar tree is first laid down.
#
# Checked against the published 1.0.59 tarball (file list) and against an
# on-disk .copilot/pkg tree laid down by the CLI, reading foundry-local-sdk's
# package.json, dist/ and script/install-utils.cjs. Re-do those three reads
# before extending the date; a CLI release that starts calling adm-zip from
# dist/ invalidates the argument.
#
# Remove when the CLI pin can advance to a release whose foundry-local-sdk
# depends on adm-zip >= 0.6.0. On 2026-11-01 the entry expires and the scans exit
# 1 again: re-verify the reachability argument above, then extend the date or
# drop the entry.
CVE-2026-39244 exp:2026-11-01
